        "original_id": "85a7fa7f-0b3a-5ebb-a7c9-a77659d9259b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Canals: Champlain Canal, Warren County Canal, Glens Falls Feeder Canal\n- Places: Lake Champlain, Hudson River, New York, southwestern Ohio, Lebanon, Middletown, Glen's Falls\n\nFacts:\n- The Champlain Canal is a 60 mi canal that connects the south end of Lake Champlain to the Hudson River in New York.\n- In the mid-19th century, the Warren County Canal was a branch of the Miami and Erie Canal in southwestern Ohio that was about 20 mi long and connected Lebanon to the main canal at Middletown.\n- The Glens Falls Feeder Canal is 7 mi long and delivers water from above Glen's Falls on the Hudson River to the highest point of the Champlain Canal.",
